{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-geodesic","title":"def:pet-ch5-geodesic","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.md","line":51,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex#def:pet-ch5-geodesic","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-acceleration]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","label":"def:pet-ch5-geodesic","line":148,"source":"\\begin{definition}[geodesic; arclength parametrization]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch5-geodesic}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0188}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch5-acceleration}\n\n  A $C^\\infty$ curve $c:I\\to M$ with vanishing acceleration, $\\ddot c=0$, is a\n  \\emph{geodesic}. If $c$ is a geodesic its speed $|\\dot c|=\\sqrt{g(\\dot c,\\dot c)}$\n  is constant, since $\\frac{d}{dt}g(\\dot c,\\dot c)=2g(\\ddot c,\\dot c)=0$; equivalently\n  $c$ is parametrized proportionally to arc length. If $|\\dot c|\\equiv1$, $c$ is\n  \\emph{parametrized by arclength}. In local coordinates on $U\\subset M$, $c:I\\to U$\n  is a geodesic iff its components satisfy the second-order system\n  \\[\n    \\ddot c^k(t)=-\\dot c^l(t)\\dot c^j(t)\\,\\Gamma^k_{lj}|_{c(t)},\\qquad k=1,\\dots,n,\n  \\]\n  giving the initial-value problem $c(0)=q$, $\\dot c(0)=\\dot c^i(0)\\partial_i|_q$ for\n  specified $q\\in U$ and initial velocity.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[geodesic; arclength parametrization] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368352d67656f6465736963\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0188</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23def%3Apet-ch5-acceleration\">↗ def:pet-ch5-acceleration</a> <p></p>A <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$C^\\infty $\">$C^\\infty $</span> curve <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c:I\\to M$\">$c:I\\to M$</span> with vanishing acceleration, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\ddot c=0$\">$\\ddot c=0$</span>, is a <em>geodesic</em>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> is a geodesic its speed <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\dot c|=\\sqrt{g(\\dot c,\\dot c)}$\">$|\\dot c|=\\sqrt{g(\\dot c,\\dot c)}$</span> is constant, since <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\frac{d}{dt}g(\\dot c,\\dot c)=2g(\\ddot c,\\dot c)=0$\">$\\frac{d}{dt}g(\\dot c,\\dot c)=2g(\\ddot c,\\dot c)=0$</span>; equivalently <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> is parametrized proportionally to arc length. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\dot c|\\equiv 1$\">$|\\dot c|\\equiv 1$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> is <em>parametrized by arclength</em>. In local coordinates on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U\\subset M$\">$U\\subset M$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c:I\\to U$\">$c:I\\to U$</span> is a geodesic iff its components satisfy the second-order system <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\ddot c^k(t)=-\\dot c^l(t)\\dot c^j(t)\\, \\Gamma ^k_{lj}|_{c(t)},\\qquad k=1,\\dots ,n,  \\]\">\\[  \\ddot c^k(t)=-\\dot c^l(t)\\dot c^j(t)\\, \\Gamma ^k_{lj}|_{c(t)},\\qquad k=1,\\dots ,n,  \\]</span> giving the initial-value problem <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c(0)=q$\">$c(0)=q$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\dot c(0)=\\dot c^i(0)\\partial _i|_q$\">$\\dot c(0)=\\dot c^i(0)\\partial _i|_q$</span> for specified <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q\\in U$\">$q\\in U$</span> and initial velocity. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-acceleration","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-geodesics","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-acceleration","title":"def:pet-ch5-acceleration","label":"def:pet-ch5-acceleration"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-geodesics","title":"rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-geodesics","label":"rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-geodesics"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-local-uniqueness","title":"thm:pet-ch5-local-uniqueness","label":"thm:pet-ch5-local-uniqueness"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-local-existence","title":"thm:pet-ch5-local-existence","label":"thm:pet-ch5-local-existence"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-leaves-compact-set","title":"prop:pet-ch5-leaves-compact-set","label":"prop:pet-ch5-leaves-compact-set"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-geodesically-complete","title":"def:pet-ch5-geodesically-complete","label":"def:pet-ch5-geodesically-complete"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#ex:pet-ch5-sphere-great-circles","title":"ex:pet-ch5-sphere-great-circles","label":"ex:pet-ch5-sphere-great-circles"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05